From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: preserve APM unmap result and buffer type

The unmap callback reports the outer basic-response opcode instead of
UNMAP_REGIONS, so the synchronous waiter cannot complete. It also drops
firmware errors and clears the data handle even for a failed position
buffer unmap. Carry the existing map-type token bit through unmap,
preserve the returned opcode/status, and clear only the selected handle
on firmware success. Ignore a reply for a missing graph.

This uses the native AudioReach map token contract in audioreach.h and
q6apm.c. The reviewed upstream snapshot retains the old unmap path.
Uke OEM audio 8eb0eccb and same-SoC OnePlus 1138e00f use a
different audio graph/memory integration and supply no drop-in native
fix. No OEM code, board value or firmware selector is copied.

Caller-side DMA error recovery, stale graph-token reuse and graph lifetime
remain separate. No stream, firmware service or audio profile is enabled.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -350,8 +350,9 @@
 	struct q6apm *apm = dev_get_drvdata(dev->parent);
 	struct audioreach_graph_info *info;
 	uint32_t mem_map_handle;
+	uint32_t pos_mask = is_pos_buf ? APM_MMAP_TOKEN_MAP_TYPE_POS_BUF : 0;
 	struct gpr_pkt *pkt __free(kfree) = audioreach_alloc_apm_cmd_pkt(sizeof(*cmd),
-						APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_UNMAP_REGIONS, graph_id);
+					APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_UNMAP_REGIONS, graph_id | pos_mask);
 	if (IS_ERR(pkt))
 		return PTR_ERR(pkt);
 
@@ -1020,17 +1021,18 @@
 			wake_up(&apm->wait);
 			break;
 		case APM_CMD_SHARED_MEM_UNMAP_REGIONS:
-			apm->result.opcode = hdr->opcode;
-			apm->result.status = 0;
-			rsp = data->payload;
-
-			info = idr_find(&apm->graph_info_idr, hdr->token);
-			if (info)
-				info->mem_map_handle = 0;
-			else
-				dev_err(dev, "Error (%d) Processing 0x%08x cmd\n", result->status,
-					result->opcode);
-
+			graph_id = hdr->token & APM_MMAP_TOKEN_GID_MASK;
+			is_pos_buf = hdr->token & APM_MMAP_TOKEN_MAP_TYPE_POS_BUF;
+			info = idr_find(&apm->graph_info_idr, graph_id);
+			if (!info)
+				break;
+			if (!result->status) {
+				if (is_pos_buf)
+					info->pos_buf_mem_map_handle = 0;
+				else
+					info->mem_map_handle = 0;
+			}
+			apm->result = *result;
 			wake_up(&apm->wait);
 			break;
 		default:
